BT /F1 10 Tf 12 TL 56 760 Td (Foodbank Fridge) Tj T* () Tj T* (Foodbank Fridge) Tj T* (Executive Summary) Tj T* () Tj T* (Problem) Tj T* () Tj T* (Restaurants, caterers, and campus dining operations throw away large amounts of edible prepared) Tj T* (food every day, mostly because they have no quick and safe way to get it to people who could) Tj T* (eat it. At the same time, many households in our own city skip meals or rely on food pantries) Tj T* (that keep limited hours and often lack fresh or prepared items. Community refrigerators have) Tj T* (appeared in some neighborhoods as a response, but most are informal. They are stocked) Tj T* (unpredictably, nobody monitors whether food has stayed cold, and neighbors cannot tell in) Tj T* (advance whether anything is inside. Donors worry about liability and about whether their food) Tj T* (will reach anyone at all. The result is that surplus food and hungry neighbors exist within a) Tj T* (few blocks of each other and still do not connect.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Solution) Tj T* () Tj T* (Foodbank Fridge combines a physical refrigerator, a software layer, and a routing service. The) Tj T* (refrigerator is a commercial-grade unit paired with a small solar panel and battery that offset) Tj T* (its power draw and keep it running through short outages, which lowers the cost of hosting it.) Tj T* (Sensors inside each unit record temperature and door activity and send readings to our) Tj T* (dashboard every few minutes. If the unit leaves the safe range for too long, the system alerts) Tj T* (a local volunteer steward and marks the contents for removal.) Tj T* () Tj T* (The app serves three groups. Donors, meaning restaurants and caterers, post available food with) Tj T* (a short description and a pickup or drop-off window. Our routing service matches the donation) Tj T* (to the nearest fridge with space and notifies nearby registered neighbors. Neighbors browse) Tj T* (what is currently available, reserve items, and pick them up without needing to prove need or) Tj T* (fill out paperwork. Stewards, typically staff or volunteers at the host site, confirm) Tj T* (deliveries and check the unit.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Market) Tj T* () Tj T* (We see three groups of customers. The first is food donors. The United States has several) Tj T* (hundred thousand restaurants, and a meaningful share of them have regular surplus. Our initial) Tj T* (focus is independent restaurants and caterers within a few miles of campus. The second is host) Tj T* (sites such as community centers, houses of worship, and housing complexes that want a food) Tj T* (resource without running a full pantry. The third is institutions, such as city agencies,) Tj T* (health systems, and universities, that fund food access and sustainability programs and need) Tj T* (reporting on results. We have not completed a formal market sizing. Using rough national) Tj T* (figures for restaurant count and food waste, we believe the long-term opportunity is large, but) Tj T* (our near-term market is the set of restaurants and host sites in our metropolitan area, which) Tj T* (we estimate at a few hundred potential donors.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Business Model) Tj T* () Tj T* (We plan to earn revenue from several sources. Donors would pay a monthly subscription for the) Tj T* (app, routing, and a donation record they can use for tax documentation and sustainability) Tj T* (reporting. Host sites or sponsors would pay a placement fee or a lease for the fridge unit.) Tj T* (Institutional partners would pay for data reports on food rescued, locations served, and) Tj T* (temperature compliance. We also expect to apply for grants during the early period. Our working) Tj T* (assumption is a donor subscription in the range of twenty to forty dollars per month and a) Tj T* (sponsor fee of a few hundred dollars per unit per year, though we have not yet tested what) Tj T* (customers will actually pay. At present the service is free to everyone, so we have no revenue.) Tj T* (A key open question is whether restaurants see enough value to pay, since many already donate) Tj T* (informally at no cost.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Competition) Tj ET
endstream
