BT /F1 10 Tf 12 TL 56 760 Td () Tj T* (The space is crowded. Food rescue organizations and apps already connect restaurants and) Tj T* (grocers with charities, and some work at large scale. Traditional food banks and pantries have) Tj T* (established relationships, trucks, and funding. Community fridge networks run by volunteers) Tj T* (offer a similar physical presence at near-zero cost. Surplus-food marketplaces sell discounted) Tj T* (food to consumers rather than giving it away. We think our difference is the combination of) Tj T* (monitored cold storage, neighborhood-level routing, and a safety record in a single product,) Tj T* (which most of these alternatives do not offer together. We recognize that a larger organization) Tj T* (could add similar features, and that volunteer-run fridges may be good enough for many) Tj T* (neighborhoods. Our advantage today is speed and a focus on temperature safety, not any) Tj T* (protected technology.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Team) Tj T* () Tj T* (Marisol Venkataraman, chief executive, studies public health and leads partnerships with) Tj T* (restaurants and host sites. She volunteered for two years at a campus food pantry. Dexter) Tj T* (Oyelaran, chief technology officer, studies computer science and built the app, the sensor data) Tj T* (pipeline, and the routing logic. Priya Halloran-Wu, chief operating officer, studies mechanical) Tj T* (engineering and designed the solar and battery configuration and the fridge enclosure. We have) Tj T* (a faculty advisor in the school of public health who has offered feedback on food safety) Tj T* (practice, and we are looking for additional mentors with experience in food service regulation) Tj T* (and nonprofit partnerships. All three of us are full-time students and are working on the) Tj T* (company alongside coursework.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Milestones and Financials) Tj T* () Tj T* (We have defined the core concept, formed a Delaware C corporation, and launched a basic) Tj T* (website. We built a working prototype of the fridge with solar assist and sensors, and the) Tj T* (first unit has been operating at a partner community center for about six weeks. During that) Tj T* (time, a handful of restaurants and several dozen neighbors have signed up and used the app. We) Tj T* (have logged the temperature readings and recorded a small number of alerts, all of which were) Tj T* (resolved without food loss. We do not yet have a rigorous count of meals rescued, and our early) Tj T* (user numbers are small and come largely from people we recruited personally.) Tj T* () Tj T* (So far we have spent roughly six thousand dollars, funded by personal savings and a small) Tj T* (student innovation grant, mostly on the fridge, panel, battery, and sensors. Our estimated cost) Tj T* (for each additional unit is between three and four thousand dollars including installation. We) Tj T* (expect to need around twenty-five thousand dollars over the next year to build several more) Tj T* (units, improve the app, and pay for insurance and basic legal work. Revenue projections beyond) Tj T* (that point depend on assumptions we still need to validate, so we are not presenting detailed) Tj T* (forecasts in this summary.) Tj T* () Tj T* (What We Are Asking For) Tj T* () Tj T* (We are applying for prize funding to build a second and third unit and extend our pilot to more) Tj T* (neighborhoods. Beyond money, we would value introductions to restaurant owners and health) Tj T* (department contacts, advice on liability and food donation law, and feedback from judges on) Tj T* (pricing. Over the coming months, our goal is to show that donors will pay for the service, that) Tj T* (neighbors return to use it, and that we can operate several units safely without a large) Tj T* (volunteer effort. We believe the competition would help us move from an interesting prototype) Tj T* (toward a business with evidence behind it.) Tj ET
